; onehotc_charge_before_expand: ONEHOTC on a model register is charged its
; expansion before it expands, so an exhausted budget decides the fault.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md charges ONEHOTR and ONEHOTC "the expansion over the row's
; or column's variables, sized from a model register", ahead of the work it
; prices ("Expansions are charged their worst case, before they expand").
; The model below is nine binary variables (72 bytes at the variable rate)
; under a budget of exactly 72, gridded 3x3. Column 0 is in range, so the
; only fault left is the charge: three linear entries and three pairs,
; 3x32 + 3x48 = 240 bytes, which the budget cannot pay.
;
; onehotc_sample_charged_nothing is the twin on a sample register, which is
; charged nothing and reaches the type check instead.

PUSH 9
BQMX r0          ; 72 bytes: the whole budget
PUSH 3
PUSH 3
RESIZE r0        ; 3x3 grid
PUSH 0           ; col, in range
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ONEHOTC r0
HALT
